-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ט/2: הסכם בענין הרפורמות במכללות להכשרת עובדי הוראה — מתוקן
-- The circular publishes the collective agreement of 21.1.2019 for teachers
-- in the teacher-training colleges (§§1–9): promotion grades replaced by
-- academic ranks, a trailing promotion supplement, a shekel supplement by
-- rank, the 2015 and 2018 one-time grants and the reform-implementation
-- grant on leaving; and adds the jubilee grant at 25 years (§10).
--
-- The agreement's rules are encoded in its own file
-- (l4/agreements/teachers-general/2019-01-21_teachers_michlalot-reform-amendment.l4),
-- which this circular imports: a circular applies the agreement and does
-- not re-encode it (MMS-521, MMS-663). Each row of §§2–9 is cited "as in
-- the agreement of 21.1.2019", by the rule that encodes it there; §10, the
-- circular's own, is encoded here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common
IMPORT `2019-01-21_teachers_michlalot-reform-amendment`
IMPORT minimum_wage_law
IMPORT womens_work_law

-- Time in the regulative rules is counted in salary months from September
-- 2018 (= 1): January 2019 is 5, February 6, May 9, June 10, July 11.

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘משרה מלאה’ and
-- ‘היקף משרה’ here measure the position, as the base of a sum paid pro rata
-- to it or a threshold of eligibility; they set no working hour, day or
-- week, nor the pay of an hour the law counts.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: the words the search found are
-- not on its subject: ‘בעל’ is holding or having (‘בעל דרגה’), not a
-- husband; none gives pay or other remuneration by sex.

§ `חוזר תשע"ט/2 הרפורמות במכללות`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference, addressee, subject, the recital of the agreement of 21.1.2019 and of the colleges' reform agreement of 7.5.2015, the circular's purpose, and the page footer (the office's address, in Hebrew and Arabic); no rule.

§§ `1 הוראות כלליות`

-- akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_c akn:art_1__para_d Rules of interpretation (the preamble is part of the agreement; gender and number; headings are for convenience); no rule to encode.

-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §5(א)(4) and (ד)(2)(ד)(5)
-- counts the trailing promotion grade supplement and the shekel supplement
-- in the wage severance is computed on, and §7(ח) leaves the 2015 grant out
-- of it. Which components count, §13 sends to the regulations, which
-- compute that wage by the collective agreement that applies (as the
-- takanon's §1.28.2.3 brings them): a component counted adds to the
-- severance, and for one left out the agreement's word is what the law
-- looks to; §13ב's minimum-wage floor holds whatever is counted.

