-- akn:art_5/p1 The recital of why the structure of pay and employment changes; no rule.
-- akn:art_7/p1 The 2015 grant's own heading, under §7's; no rule of its own.

-- The Women's Work Law (through the agreement of 21.1.2019): §7(ה) and
-- (ז) count a month of the birth and parenthood period for the grant, as
-- unpaid leave after it is not, and §7(ו) takes the position on its eve.
-- The period harms no right that turns on seniority (§6(ט)). The floor is
-- met.
`§7 of תשע"ט/2 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it` MEANS
    `§7 of 21.1.2019 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it`
#ASSERT `§7 of תשע"ט/2 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it`

-- Against the Minimum Wage Law's floor (MMS-601): §7(ט) leaves the 2015 grant out;
-- leaving it out of the pay that counts toward the top-up makes the
-- top-up the law's or more (its §11). Checked on a month's figures as if
-- §3 counted it (a fixed supplement for the work), the strictest case.
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the one-time grants count for` `topping up to the minimum wage`)

§§ `10 מענק יובל`

-- §10: from the June 2016 salary (the jubilee grant for תשע"ו) the
-- seniority for the jubilee grant (section 11 of the agreement of
-- 19.9.1994) is 25 years, not 30; its other rules are unchanged; the
-- differences are paid in the May 2019 salary (9), at the latest June's (10).
@ref akn:art_10/p1
GIVEN `paid with the salary of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee seniority in the colleges` `paid with the salary of` IS
    IF `paid with the salary of` AT LEAST Date 1 6 2016 THEN 25 ELSE 30

@ref akn:art_10/p2
GIVEN `differences owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `college action`
DECIDE `paying the jubilee differences` `differences owed` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the jubilee differences` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `differences owed`
    WITHIN 10
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 10: the differences by the June 2019 salary at the latest"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, the signatures and signatories, and the copies list; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2018-19_tashat_02-a: at 65 years and 6 months the table's last row
-- gives 35,000 if "עד גיל 65" runs, like the rows above it, to 65 and 11
-- months, and nothing if it ends at 65.
`the last row read to 65 and 11 months` MEANS `age band` 768 791 35000
`the two readings of "up to 65" differ at 65 and a half` MEANS
        `the table's special grant` 786 EQUALS 0
    AND 786 AT MOST `the last row read to 65 and 11 months`'s `to age in months`
#ASSERT `the two readings of "up to 65" differ at 65 and a half`

§§ `Property checks`

-- §10: the colleges' jubilee seniority is 25 years exactly from the June
-- 2016 salary, 30 before.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `the jubilee seniority in the colleges` d EQUALS (IF d AT LEAST Date 1 6 2016 THEN 25 ELSE 30))
            (LIST Date 1 5 2016, Date 1 6 2016, Date 1 6 2019)
